  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "A party-planning company decorated a room with $200$ balloons. Of this amount, $7.5%$ of the balloons are white. How many white balloons are there?",
  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the number of balloons in the room, which is $200.$ The percentage is $7.5%,$ and the part is the number of white balloons.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n7.5%=7.5÷100=0.075\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7.5%\\times 200 \\\\  & =0.075\\times 200 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7.5%$ of $200$ is $15.$ Thus, there are $15$ white balloons.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n7.5%=\\frac{7.5}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7.5%\\times 200 \\\\  & =\\frac{7.5}{100}\\times 200 \\\\  & =7.5\\times \\frac{200}{100} \\\\  & =7.5\\times 2 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7.5%$ of $200$ is $15.$ Thus, there are $15$ white balloons.",
